nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:11:#    [SystemSettings]\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:12:#    Electra.Win.H264UseOldOutputPath=1\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:13:#    Electra.Win.H265UseOldOutputPath=1\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:14:#  See WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md for the exact per-game setup.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:15:#\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:16:#  USAGE:\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:17:#    1. Duplicate your CrossOver.app (keep the original pristine).\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:18:#    2. Run:  ./patch.sh /path/to/CrossOver-copy.app  [bottle ...]\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:19:#       - no bottle args  -> patches the APP + EVERY existing bottle\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:20:#       - bottle args      -> patches the APP + only those bottles\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:21:#\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:22:#  STAGING (no admin / no Full Disk Access needed): if the path you pass does\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:23:#  NOT end in \".app\" (e.g. \".../CrossOver-winevideo\"), it is treated as a plain\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:24:#  staging folder. macOS \"App Management\" only protects real .app bundles, so a\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:25:#  folder can be patched + signed as the normal user with no elevation; this\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:26:#  script then renames it to \"<name>.app\" at the very end. The GUI uses this.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:27:#\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:28:#  The APP-level DLLs apply to all bottles. The per-bottle registry (VP9 decoder\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:29:#  + .webm/.mkv/.msd handlers) is required and is stamped into each bottle.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:30:#  Re-run with a bottle name to patch a newly-created bottle later.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:31:#\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:32:#  Reversible:  ./restore.sh /path/to/CrossOver-copy.app [bottle ...]\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:33:# =============================================================================\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:41:# Optional mode flag (must be first). Kept for compatibility / CLI:\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:42:#   --app-only    = only patch the app files (+ finalize/rename)\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:43:#   --bottle-only = only register the per-bottle registry (app must already be .app)\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:44:# The GUI uses neither: it passes a staging folder and lets MODE=all do everything.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:48:APP=\"${1:-}\"\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:54:# Staging detection: a path without a .app extension is a staging folder we will\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:55:# rename to <name>.app after patching+signing. FINAL is the eventual .app path;\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:56:# the backup is always keyed off FINAL so restore.sh finds it.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:60:# Optional RE Engine / extra codecs come from the USER's own official GStreamer 1.24.x\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:61:# framework (we never ship FFmpeg). If it isn't installed, that step is simply skipped.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:75:# Remove quarantine so macOS doesn't SIGKILL (\"Killed: 9\") the wine binaries in a\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:76:# copied/downloaded bundle. NEVER codesign --deep the app: that strips CrossOver's\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:77:# entitlements (JIT / executable memory) and Wine silently stops working. We only\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:78:# ad-hoc sign the individual dylibs we add (fix_so) + re-seal the top bundle.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:83:# Repoint a .so/.dylib's @rpath gst/glib refs to the app's lib64, compat-rewrite\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:84:# framework (2414) versions to CX26.2 (2405/glib 7801), ad-hoc sign.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:85:# IMPORTANT: the rpath must point to lib64 in the FINAL location, not where the file\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:86:# physically sits during patching. When staging, files are patched in a folder that is\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:87:# then renamed to .app — an absolute rpath to the folder would dangle after the rename.\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:88:# So we add (1) a @loader_path-relative rpath (relocation-proof: survives the rename AND\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:89:# the user later moving/renaming the app) and (2) the absolute final-.app lib64 as a\nTools/CrossOverWinevideoPatcher/winevideo Patcher.app/Contents/Resources/patch.sh:90:# belt-and-suspenders fallback (this matches the proven pre-staging behavior).\n"},"started_at_ms":1787725485364,"completed_at_ms":1787725485364}}
